  "source": "The Swedish Council for Information on Alcohol and Other Drugs (CAN)",
  "note": [
    "Indicator definition: Percentage (%) of the population (17-84 years) that stated that once per week or more often they are indoor in premises where others smoke or have recently smoked. In 2013 STAD conducted a questionnaire (baseline measurement) on uses and consequences among the Swedish population with respect to alcohol, narcotics, doping and tobacco. The data collection took place through a survey (postal or online survey) targeted to a nationally representative sample of the population. In total 15,576 persons participated in the survey, which corresponded to a response rate of 59.3%."
  ]
